course: dictionary
lesson: 5828
title: A French word in English
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Maillot is a French word, and English has borrowed it for some clothes. You can use context to work out its meaning. «Le maillot jaune is the yellow jersey worn by the rider leading the whole race» tells you that maillot names a top, and that the race leader wears it.
explain: The other words in a phrase are clues too. «Jaune» means yellow, and «de bain» means for bathing. So «un maillot de bain» must be a swimsuit. Swap your meaning into the sentence: a yellow top worn by the leader makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Context also tells you what the yellow jersey is not. The leader wears it because he is ahead in the race, not because it is his team's colour. A good reader notices the reason given in the sentence.
fact: Maillot is a French word, and English uses it too.
fact: «Maillot» means a jersey or top worn by cyclists.
fact: In the Tour de France, «le maillot jaune» is the yellow jersey worn by the rider leading the race.
fact: «Maillot» can also mean a one-piece swimsuit, or tight clothes for dancers and gymnasts.
fact: «Un maillot de bain» means a swimsuit or swimming trunks in French.
exercise: «Le maillot jaune is the yellow jersey worn by the rider leading the whole race.» What is a maillot? | A bicycle wheel | *A jersey or top worn by cyclists | A French train ticket
exercise: In French, «un maillot de bain» is what? | A cycling helmet | A bath towel | *A swimsuit or swimming trunks
exercise: Why does the rider wear the yellow jersey in the Tour de France? | Because it is raining | Because he is the oldest rider | Because it is his team's colour | *Because he is leading the race
test: Which word means a one-piece swimsuit or tight clothes for dancers and gymnasts? | chapeau | baguette | *maillot
test: What colour is «maillot jaune»? | Blue | Red | Green | *Yellow
exam: In French, what does «maillot de bain» mean? | A pair of shoes | A bicycle | *A swimsuit | A yellow jersey
